"Osric weighs with a heavy pound and calls the sacks light, so a tenth of 74 came to 9 sacks last year."
"Osric sells the grain he skims to a Bramwick meal-merchant, in small lots, through a cousin."
"Osric has skimmed four villages for six years, and has never been challenged by a headman."
"Osric would rather abandon a village's tithe than let a reckoner read his book aloud."
"Osric's escort would kill a mortal who laid hands on Osric, and Osric would not stop him."
"Osric is afraid of nothing in Ashford except a written record he did not make."
